    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d908">

                <pb facs="0856" n="846" xml:id="pg846"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2455: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-08T10:00:00+07:00">April 8, 1941—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 8—9:06 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“The decision of the Chinese Government communicated to you on April 4<anchor
                            n="97" xml:id="d908-f1"/> was based upon the assumption that the
                        provisions of the land regulations concerning the number and nationality of
                        the councilors would be suspended for a period not exceeding 2 years.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Sent to Shanghai, repeated to Department and Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d908-f1" n="97" xml:id="d908-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram of April 4, 6 p.m., <ref target="#pg844">p. 844</ref>.</p>
            </note>
